00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:21.240
Niko: Yaaaay

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:23.240
*clapping*

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:24.620
Sam: Its 4 Million Subs Eve

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:27.380
It was... It was a cold and dark september 2nd

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:29.920
All was well on 4 Million Subs Eve

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:30.720
Niko: Here is you guys

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:32.080
All 4 Million of you

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:33.020
Sam: All 4 Million

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:35.760
4 Million Subs Eve

00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:48.420
Jake: The story of the Corridor Digital air conditioner started in 2011

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:50.700
In a loft, in Los Angeles, California

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:55.780
Where it was myself, Sam and Niko, and we were working, and it was 95ºF (35ºC)

00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:58.180
We said, you know what? We don't have the money right now

00:00:58.340 --> 00:01:00.780
We rather just go, and deal with it

00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:06.200
And now, 5 years later, we finally decided to bite the bullet and pay for the air conditioning

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:08.440
And I gotta tell you, we were just out shooting today

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:12.160
It was super hot, and we get back, and its nice and cool in here

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:13.460
It is worth every penny

00:01:13.720 --> 00:01:16.600
We learned a couple things from stress level zero

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:18.840
In the process of getting this air conditioning

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:21.060
Because the guy that we have over there...

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:23.400
Well... I don't gotta tell you guys

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:29.080
Wren: We have an issue, there is a pipe on the tool room that is leaking water all over the shelves

00:01:29.620 --> 00:01:30.720
Jake: In our tool room?

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:31.880
Wren: Yes

00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:34.800
Jake: How many AC units do you have to install

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:37.420
Were 2 out of the 3 leak water

00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:39.760
We could just be dumping water somewhere

00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:42.520
How is this OK? Now what do we do with these?

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:45.020
Now, we found a new guy, his name's Aswaldo

00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:47.900
Aswaldo Marisco hooked it up he did a great job

00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:51.420
He actually took the time and detail to do things properly on the roof

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:53.020
Even though you can't see that

00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:56.420
That thing is pumping out, sweet sweet cool air

00:01:56.420 --> 00:02:01.040
And our pump's not leaking because he took the time to get a bigger one and to put it in the wall

00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:03.780
And it doesn't look too damn bad either

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:07.540
The future now it's bright at Corridor Digital, it's soo bright

00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:09.120
I know this are first world problems OK?

00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:11.800
Even without air conditioning we still got it made in the shade

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:13.940
But the point is: It's been a long journey

00:02:13.940 --> 00:02:16.560
And we worked for it, and we worked for it, and we worked for it

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:19.900
There are 3 things that I will remember in my life time when I'm on my death bed

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:22.420
Number 1, the day that my kid it's gonna be born

00:02:22.420 --> 00:02:24.240
Number 2, the day that I got married

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:27.420
And number 3, the day that we got air conditioning in Corridor Digital

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:29.580
Wren: And the day you met me!

00:02:30.620 --> 00:02:32.120
Jake: And the day I met Wren

